#HELPS

0 MORPH DRAGONFORM~
Syntax: morph
Dragon-form toggle for Dragons; MORPH is the registered command name.
Entering uses your Dragon color/age, clears native combat modifiers and
enables learned claws, horns, wings, fangs and nightsight.
Leaving retracts those active Dragon features, removes its form flags
and restores native style. An unrelated polymorph can prevent changing.
It does not change your permanent parent class.
~

0 BREATH DBREATH~
Syntax: breath [room target]
Dragon must learn Breath through DRAGONSKILL and be in Dragon form.
Uses the current opponent first, otherwise the named room target.
After native safety checks it performs the Dragon breath combat attack
and applies its wait. This is not CAST 'fire breath' or another callback.
~

0 DUST~
Syntax: dust [room target]
Dragon must learn Dust, be in Dragon form and have its wings extended.
Uses the current opponent first, otherwise the named room target.
After safety checks it can remove a player's holy-light flag and applies
native blindness with -50 hitroll if not already blind; command wait applies.
~

0 STAIL~
Syntax: stail [room target]
Dragon must learn Tail and be in Dragon form.
Uses the current opponent first, otherwise the named room target.
After native safety checks it performs the spiked-tail combat attack
and applies its wait. It does not grant a permanent extra parent class.
~

0 HORNS DRAGONHORNS~
Syntax: horns
Dragon learned-horns toggle. Extension requires Dragon form; retraction
is allowed for already extended horns. The native combat loop uses
extended horns for its chance of an additional piercing attack.
Demon class-prefixed horn powers are separate adapters.
~

0 WINGS DRAGONWINGS~
Syntax: wings
Dragon must learn Wings and be in Dragon form.
Toggles extended Dragon wings. Extended wings permit native air-sector
travel, enable Dust and give the native combat loop its wing-buffet chance.
This is separate from Angel wings, Cyborg propulsion and the Fly spell.
~

0 DRAGONSKILL~
Syntax: dragonskill
        dragonskill <skill>
        dragonskill age
Lists skills unlocked by your current Dragon age, or purchases one using
Dragon Points. The skill's unlock tier determines its DP price.
AGE purchases the next native age using DP and, at later tiers, quest
points; the command reports the required resources if you cannot pay.
Purchases take effect immediately when eligible and affordable.
Existing-skill and maximum-age gates prevent duplicate advancement.
~

0 INCREASE HIGHLANDERTRAINING~
Syntax: increase
        increase <attack|defense|weaponry|powers>
Highlander progression. Each track caps at 6.
Training costs 15 times the next rank in primal and advances only that
track. The POWERS track unlocks the commands described below.
~

0 BFLASH BLADEFLASH~
Syntax: bflash <room target>
Highlander Powers 2. Attempts the native Blade Flash after safety checks.
It can remove a player's holy-light flag and applies blindness with
-50 hitroll if the victim is not already blind. Command wait applies.
The registered command is BFLASH, not BLADEFLASH.
~

0 BASH~
Syntax: bash [room target]
Highlander Powers 3. Uses the current opponent first, then a named target.
Through native hostile-combat checks it attempts 851-950 damage and
additional victim wait on a hit. It has a native miss chance; qualifying
Lupus Werewolves have an additional avoidance chance. Caster wait applies.
~

0 HTWIST~
Syntax: htwist
Highlander Powers 4. Adds five times Powers rank to native celerity.
It refuses when already using increased speed (celerity greater than 1).
This is the native speed counter, not permanent stats or a new resource.
~

0 JUDGE JUDGEMENT~
Syntax: judge <room target>
Highlander Powers 5. Reports native NPC/player status, approximate health
and mana rounded down to 2000-point units, and derived armor.
It is informational, not damage or player-alignment reading.
The registered command is JUDGE.
~

0 LUNGE~
Syntax: lunge <room target>
Highlander Powers 6. Rejects self and native protected targets, starts
combat if necessary and drops the victim's active fighting stance.
It applies caster wait; this command does not itself make a damage roll.
~

0 FORGE~
Syntax: forge
        forge <owned carried weapon>
Highlander crafting costs 50 primal and 100 quest points.
With no argument it creates the native aggravated katana.
With a weapon it REPLACES that owned, non-artifact/non-relic weapon with
the katana template and copies its four native weapon values.
The original is consumed: other names, flags and custom object affects
are NOT copied. Claim/ownership and the native template must be valid.
This is not Sorcerer enchantment or a lossless equipment upgrade.
~

